What I checked: `RecordsRepository.ts` (8 methods, parameterized SQL, overlap semantics, JS stats, 1-statement `delete()`), `validate.ts`, the 5 route handlers (all ≤10 lines, `/stats` before `/:id`), MockD1 overlap predicate, and the migrated `records/klines/admin` tests.

Key outcome: the prior HIGH (partial `PUT` resetting `msb:'yes'` via Zod v4 `.partial()` injecting the baseFields default) is genuinely fixed by `e66251f` and locked in by regression tests `83205ec` + `7f7bf54` — both pass. The `update()` concurrent-delete guard (fix-3) is present but untested.

Findings in the final state: **0 CRITICAL, 0 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, 4 LOW**. The MEDIUM is a pre-existing latent bug now owned by the repository: a `PUT` sending only `start_time` (or only `end_time`) bypasses the refine (which checks only when both are present) and can persist `start_time >= end_time`, breaking overlap queries. API-level trigger only — the UI always sends both times. LOWs: fix-3 `changes===0` branch untested, MockD1 lacks column projection (masks `queryKlines` projection bugs, test-only), `findByTimeRange` doesn't validate `start <= end`, and a pre-existing permissive CORS default now also covers `/stats`.

